// input: after idr-simplify
// FILECHECK-OPTIONS: --implicit-check-not={{[^#]}}idr.closure --implicit-check-not=idr.apply
// rule: ELIM-SPEC-1, ELIM-G-1, TEST-ELIM-1
// One copy of iter per static function argument: iter is partial, but its
// calls are not closed (n comes from stdin), so each is specialized on the
// closure it passes, whose label is the key. The original iter is dead
// and removed, and in each copy the closure is known, so it is applied as
// a call and inlined: no closure is left. Each copy computes with its own
// function, in either order (two copies with the same function would share
// one key, so they would be one copy).
// CHECK: func.func private @Main.iter$spec${{[0-9]+}}(
// CHECK: arith.{{addi|muli}}
// CHECK: func.func private @Main.iter$spec${{[0-9]+}}(
// CHECK: arith.{{addi|muli}}
// CHECK-NOT: func.func private @Main.iter
